('FR-055:BE-01','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','BE-01','BE','Extends IceRunContext.load(runId) to read the responsive_config JSON column from the run_execution row. Populates ctx.responsiveViewports() as a List<ResponsiveViewport> enum (DW_LARGE=1440px, DW_REGULAR=1280px, DW_SMALL=360px, TABLET=768px). Returns empty list if no responsive checkboxes were selected — ResponsiveWorker skips gracefully when list is empty.',0.5,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:BE-02','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','BE-02','BE','Implements GspecCache — a @BeforeClass component that pulls all .gspec files for the current journey from Git at test startup. Path convention: gspec/{tenantId}/{journeyId}/{screenName}.gspec. Also pulls screens.json (the screen name manifest ICE publishes). Caches files to a local temp directory for the duration of the run. Cleaned up in @AfterClass. If a .gspec file does not exist for a screen, the cache returns null and ResponsiveWorker skips that screen gracefully.',0.75,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:BE-03','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','BE-03','BE','Implements ScreenManifestPublisher — generates and pushes screens.json to Git whenever ICE generates or updates journey scripts (FR-019). screens.json lists all screen names used in the journey so manual .gspec authors know exactly what names to use. Also pushes an empty .gspec template for each screen as a starting point for manual authors. screens.json format: {"journeyId": "J-001", "screens": ["login_page", "accounts_page", ...], "generatedAt": "2026-04-30T00:00:00Z"}.',0.75,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:BE-04','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','BE-04','BE','Implements ResponsiveWorker — the async validation worker for Galen-based responsive testing. Receives PageSnapshot + IceRunContext. For each viewport in ctx.responsiveViewports(): looks up .gspec from GspecCache by snapshot.screenName(). If no .gspec found, skips. Otherwise: launches isolated headless Chromium via Playwright Java at the viewport width, loads snapshot.pageUrl(), calls GalenApi.checkLayout(driver, specFile, viewportTag). Collects GalenTestInfo results and passes to BE-05 writer. Disposes headless browser after each viewport check.',1.88,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:BE-05','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','BE-05','BE','Extends VisualResultWriter to handle responsive (Galen) results. Writes one visual_diff_results row per viewport per screen per run. Adds a viewport column and galen_report_json column to the existing visual_diff_results table via Flyway migration. Also writes a summary InfluxDB measurement (responsive_check) with tags: tenantId, journeyId, screenName, viewport — and fields: passCount, failCount, skipCount, durationMs.',0.94,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:BE-06','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','BE-06','BE','Extends the FR-022 run execution API to store viewport selections. Adds a responsive_config JSONB column to run_execution table via Flyway migration. The POST /api/v1/run/execute endpoint accepts a responsiveViewports string array in the request body. BE stores these as {"viewports": ["DW_LARGE", "DW_SMALL"]} in responsive_config. If no viewports selected, stores null — script will skip all responsive checks.',0.5,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:FE-01','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','FE-01','FE','Wires the existing viewport checkboxes (FR-022 FE-06: DW Large / DW Regular / DW Small / Tablet) to the POST /api/v1/run/execute request body. When the user clicks Run, the selected checkbox values are included in responsiveViewports[] in the payload. If no checkboxes are ticked, responsiveViewports is omitted from the payload. No new UI components needed — FR-022 FE-06 already renders the checkboxes. This task only adds the wiring to the run payload.',0.25,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:INT-01','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','INT-01','INT','Validates the Figma-driven path end-to-end: FR-047 generates .gspec from Figma -> pushed to Git -> journey script runs with DW_SMALL + DW_LARGE selected -> GspecCache pulls .gspec at startup -> ResponsiveWorker runs Galen checks at both viewports -> results written to visual_diff_results and InfluxDB. Test 1: PASS — valid .gspec, all elements in correct positions. Test 2: FAIL — element outside bounds at DW_SMALL. Test 3: skip — no .gspec for a screen, verify graceful skip. Test 4: InfluxDB assertion — responsive_check measurement written with correct viewport tag.',1.5,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:INT-02','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','INT-02','INT','Validates the manual .gspec path end-to-end: developer pushes hand-authored .gspec to Git -> ICE publishes screens.json (BE-03) -> journey script runs -> GspecCache pulls manually authored .gspec -> ResponsiveWorker runs Galen checks -> results written. Also validates screens.json generation (BE-03): correct screen names listed, idempotent re-run does not overwrite manually authored spec.',0.94,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-055:BE-07','FR-055','Responsive Testing Engine (Galen)','BE-07','BE','Updates the FR-019 journey script generator to inject two lifecycle hooks and conditional RESPONSIVE validation into every generated script that has responsive viewports configured. Adds GspecCache.init(ctx) call to the @BeforeClass template, GspecCache.cleanup() to the @AfterClass template, and conditionally appends RESPONSIVE to the ValidationType[] array in each ValidationRunner.fireAsync() call — but only when the journey config includes at least one responsive viewport. Scripts generated for journeys with no responsive config are unchanged.',0.5,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-056:BE-01','FR-056','Network Performance Capture & Analysis','BE-01','BE','Implements the network capture pipeline that attaches a Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) listener to the active ChromeDriver session when ice.network.start(driver) is called. Captures all Network.requestWillBeSent, Network.responseReceived, and Network.loadingFinished CDP events. Parses raw CDP events into structured NetworkRequest records containing url, method, status_code, dns_ms, connect_ms, ssl_ms, ttfb_ms, download_ms, total_ms, request_size_bytes, response_size_bytes, resource_type, and screen_label.',2.5,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-056:BE-02','FR-056','Network Performance Capture & Analysis','BE-02','BE','Creates the network_results PostgreSQL table (19 columns, 90-day retention) and the network_request InfluxDB measurement (bucket: ice-network, 30-day retention). Also adds 4 aggregate network fields to the existing test_result InfluxDB measurement (total_requests, avg_api_ttfb_ms, slowest_request_ms, total_transfer_kb) present when test_type = network.',1.25,'dep_on',18),
('FR-056:BE-03','FR-056','Network Performance Capture & Analysis','BE-03','BE','Creates the network_performance_config table and implements Settings › Network Performance backend. Stores per-tenant: api_response_threshold_ms (default 2000ms), capture_resources bool (XHR/Fetch/Document only vs all resources), and enabled flag. Adds network_performance_enabled column to library_config. Threshold is applied during BE-01 flush to set threshold_exceeded flag.',0.94,'needs_fr',18),
('FR-056:BE-04','FR-056','Network Performance Capture & Analysis','BE-04','BE','Implements 3 analytics query endpoints powering the Network tab: (1) /requests — waterfall data grouped by screen_label for latest run; (2) /slowest — top 10 requests by total_ms; (3) /trend — InfluxDB aggregate network fields across last 10 runs. All tenant-scoped, 1s SLA, empty array not 404.',1.25,'dep_on',18),
('FR-056:FE-01','FR-056','Network Performance Capture & Analysis','FE-01','FE','Renders Settings › Network Performance screen: Enable toggle (maps to library_config.network_performance_enabled), API Response Threshold input (ms, default 2000, range 100–30000), Capture All Resources toggle (default off). Follows existing Settings screen component pattern.',0.94,'dep_on',18),
('FR-056:FE-02','FR-056','Network Performance Capture & Analysis','FE-02','FE','Renders the Network tab in Analytics Dashboard: (1) Waterfall panel — per-screen collapsible sections, each request as a colour-coded horizontal bar (DNS=grey, Connect=yellow, SSL=orange, TTFB=blue, Download=green); SLOW=amber highlight, ERROR=red. (2) Slowest Requests table — top 10 sortable by total_ms/ttfb_ms. (3) Trend chart — Recharts LineChart of avg_api_ttfb_ms across last 10 runs.',1.88,'dep_on',18),
('FR-056:INT-01','FR-056','Network Performance Capture & Analysis','INT-01','INT','Full E2E validation: SDK attaches CDP listener → test run executes → records flushed → network_results and InfluxDB populated → Analytics Network tab renders correctly. Verified across Java and C# SDKs.',1.25,'dep_on',18),
('FR-057:BE-01','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','BE-01','BE','Creates all DB schema objects for FR-057: security_findings PG table (per-finding, per-screen, per-run), cve_library_index PG table (bundled NVD + Retire.js CVE data), security_config PG table (per-tenant settings), and the security_finding InfluxDB measurement. Also adds security_enabled column to library_config.',1.25,'needs_fr',14),
('FR-057:BE-02','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','BE-02','BE','Implements the CVE library index loader that populates cve_library_index from two sources: (1) Retire.js JSON vulnerability database for JS libraries — bundled as a resource file, parsed and inserted at startup. (2) NVD (NIST National Vulnerability Database) snapshot for server-side libraries — downloaded weekly via NVD REST API v2 and upserted into cve_library_index. Weekly @Scheduled refresh job updates both sources.',1.25,'dep_on',14),
('FR-057:BE-03','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','BE-03','BE','Implements the server-side handler for ice.security.analyse(). Receives a security snapshot from the SDK and performs passive security analysis. The SDK collects: CDP response headers for the current page URL, all active cookies via Network.getAllCookies CDP command, all script src URLs via JS execution, and the current page URL. The server checks this snapshot against the 11 passive security rules and writes findings.',1.88,'needs_fr',14),
('FR-057:BE-04','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','BE-04','BE','Implements the PassiveRuleEngine that runs 11 passive security checks against the SecuritySnapshot and writes findings to security_findings and InfluxDB. Rules check response headers, cookie flags, mixed content, and vulnerable JS libraries (via CveMatchService from BE-02).',1.88,'dep_on',14),
('FR-057:BE-05','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','BE-05','BE','Implements the ZAP sidecar manager. ZAP is pre-installed on the ICE agent machine (same as JMeter in FR-048). ICE starts ZAP as a daemon process via ProcessBuilder before the journey run begins, communicates with it via the ZAP REST API on localhost:8090, and triggers active scans per screen URL. After the journey completes, ICE polls ZAP for results, writes findings to security_findings, then terminates the ZAP process.',2.5,'needs_fr',14),
('FR-057:BE-06','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','BE-06','BE','Extends the FR-019 ScriptTemplateEngine to inject security hooks into generated scripts when securityEnabled=true. Injects ZapProcessManager.start() at @BeforeClass, ice.security.analyse(driver, ctx.screen("name")) at each journey step, and ZapResultsCollector.collect() + ZapProcessManager.stop() at @AfterClass. Also supersedes FR-045 BE-09: the security.start() and security.stop() methods now delegate to FR-057 BE-03 and BE-05 respectively.',0.94,'needs_fr',14),
('FR-057:BE-07','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','BE-07','BE','Implements the Settings › Security Testing backend. Manages security_config per tenant: passive_enabled toggle, zap_enabled toggle, zap_scan_policy selector, and allowed_environments multi-select. Also manages library_config.security_enabled via the same save operation.',0.94,'needs_fr',14),
('FR-057:BE-08','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','BE-08','BE','Implements 3 analytics query endpoints powering the Security tab: (1) /findings — all findings for latest run grouped by screen_label, (2) /summary — finding counts by severity and source (PASSIVE vs ZAP), (3) /trend — InfluxDB finding counts across last 10 runs. All tenant-scoped, 1s SLA, empty array not 404.',1.25,'dep_on',14),
('FR-057:FE-01','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','FE-01','FE','Renders the Settings › Security Testing screen. Enable Passive Analysis toggle, Enable ZAP Active Scanning toggle (with warning: staging/UAT only), ZAP Scan Policy selector (OWASP Top 10 / Full Scan), and Allowed Environments multi-select checkboxes.',0.94,'dep_on',14),
('FR-057:FE-02','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','FE-02','FE','Renders the Security tab in the Analytics Dashboard. Three panels: (1) Findings by Screen — collapsible sections per screen_label, each finding shows severity badge, check_type, title, evidence, remediation. Source badge: PASSIVE (blue) or ZAP (red). (2) Severity Summary — donut chart (HIGH=red, MEDIUM=amber, LOW=blue, INFO=grey) with counts. (3) Trend — line chart of total_findings and high_count across last 10 runs.',1.88,'dep_on',14),
('FR-057:INT-01','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','INT-01','INT','Full E2E for passive security analysis: SDK collects snapshot → POST /api/v1/security/analyse → PassiveRuleEngine runs 11 checks → security_findings written → InfluxDB written → Security tab renders findings.',1.25,'needs_fr',14),
('FR-057:INT-02','FR-057','Security Analysis Engine — Passive + ZAP Active Scanning','INT-02','INT','Full E2E for ZAP active scanning: ZAP daemon starts → journey runs with ice.security.analyse() → ZAP spider + activeScan triggered per URL → journey completes → ZapResultsCollector.collect() → ZAP findings written to security_findings → Security tab shows ZAP findings alongside passive findings.',1.25,'needs_fr',14),
